{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"agent_message","text":"# Review: SUGGESTIONS\n\n## Required Changes\n1. **Clutch resolution / egg progress**: The shrimp lifecycle still violates the clutch-resolution invariant.\n   - Current: [`step_daily_shrimp`](file:///root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs) calls [`spawning`]( /root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs#L250 ) before [`egg_development`]( /root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs#L298 ), uses one shared `egg_progress_days` for all berried females, then resolves all current `berried_females_count` together and resets progress to `0.0` at [shrimp.rs#L373]( /root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs#L373 ). A female that becomes berried late in the cycle, or even on the same daily tick, can therefore hatch/fail immediately with the older cohort.\n   - Expected: Only completed clutches should resolve. Later berried females need separate cohort/progress tracking or an equivalent aggregate model that preserves “only the resolved clutch leaves `berried_females_count`” and “`egg_progress_days` resets only for completed clutches.”\n   - Reference: Loop 6 acceptance criteria for “Egg development advances daily” and the clutch-resolution failure invariant.\n\n2. **`thermal_reproduction_penalty` acceptance test**: The added regression does not match the required acceptance test.\n   - Current: [`thermal_reproduction_penalty.rs`]( /root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/tests/thermal_reproduction_penalty.rs#L73 ) checks reproductive readiness after 20 days, not 60, and the day-60 assertion is weakened to `warm_total <= cool_total || warm_juveniles <= cool_juveniles` at [#L120]( /root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/tests/thermal_reproduction_penalty.rs#L120 ).\n   - Expected: After 60 days, the `30 C` tank must end with at least `20%` lower reproductive readiness and fewer juveniles than the `25 C` tank, matching the loop spec and prompt acceptance test.\n   - Reference: Prompt §14.9 `thermal_reproduction_penalty`; loop 6 acceptance criterion for the mandatory acceptance test.\n\n3. **Preset validation for new shrimp/microfauna fields**: The loop adds new data-driven runtime inputs without extending the loader validation path.\n   - Current: [`load_shrimp`]( /root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/src/lib.rs#L49 ) returns parsed TOML with no validation, and [`ProcessParamsPreset::validate`]( /root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs#L459 ) never checks the newly added shrimp/microfauna fields.\n   - Expected: Add `ShrimpPreset` validation and include the new process parameters in validation so invalid loop-6 preset data cannot silently enter deterministic runtime state.\n   - Reference: Prompt §1 deliverable for `tank_data` (“TOML preset loading and validation”); loop 6 file requirements for `crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs`.\n\n## Recommended Improvements\n1. I could not re-run the Rust test suite in this environment because `cargo` is not available on `PATH`; once the toolchain path is exposed, re-run the shrimp and save/load regressions after fixing the above."}}
