{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"agent_message","text":"# Review: APPROVED\n\n## Acceptance Criteria Checklist\n- [x] Shrimp species data is no longer inert: scenario materialization loads `shrimp_profile_id` into persisted runtime params, and preset/process validation now covers the new shrimp and microfauna fields. Evidence: [lib.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs#L236), [state.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/state.rs#L43), [lib.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/src/lib.rs#L49), [presets.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs#L117), [presets.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs#L525)\n- [x] The engine wiring matches the loop spec: hourly shrimp stress runs after chemistry/DO and before hourly event emission, and the daily order is plants -> algae/periphyton -> microfauna -> shrimp lifecycle/mortality -> biofilter/stability. Evidence: [engine.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs#L70), [engine.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs#L93), [shrimp.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs#L58)\n- [x] Shrimp and microfauna behaviors required by the spec are implemented: hourly NH3/nitrite/DO/heat/instability stress, stability tracking from temp/pH/GH/DO swings, daily condition/molt/reproduction, cohort-based egg development and hatching, deterministic mortality, periphyton grazing, and microfauna turnover/mineralization coupling. Evidence: [shrimp.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs#L10), [shrimp.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs#L84), [shrimp.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs#L250), [microfauna.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/microfauna.rs#L10), [nitrogen_cycle.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/nitrogen_cycle.rs#L70), [biology.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/biology.rs#L5)\n- [x] State validation and observability are in place: `RemoveShrimp` is queue-aware and returns a typed error without mutating state on failure, berried/adult invariants are enforced, and `TankSnapshot` exposes the shrimp and microfauna fields needed for the later TUI work. Evidence: [engine.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs#L242), [actions.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/actions.rs#L78), [invariants.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/invariants.rs#L107), [snapshot.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/snapshot.rs#L24)\n- [x] Required eventing and regression coverage are present: `ShrimpBerried`, `EggFailure`, and `MoltStressWarning` emit cause-coded events, and the added tests cover thermal reproduction penalty, berried transitions, hatch failure, combined-stress mortality, microfauna suppression, and shrimp-removal invariants. Evidence: [shrimp.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs#L293), [shrimp.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs#L372), [shrimp.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs#L478), [thermal_reproduction_penalty.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/tests/thermal_reproduction_penalty.rs#L81), [shrimp_population.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/tests/shrimp_population.rs#L71), [events.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/tests/events.rs#L128)\n\n## Notes\nThe implementation now matches the loop 6 spec and fixes the previously identified gaps: cohort-based clutch resolution, the 60-day thermal reproduction acceptance test, and preset validation were all addressed in code.\n\nI could not re-run the Rust test suite in this environment because `cargo` was not available on `PATH`, so this approval is based on static review of the committed implementation and test coverage.\n\n## Commit Message\nImplement deterministic shrimp lifecycle, microfauna turnover, and shrimp preset materialization"}}
